UPDATE `courses` SET `apply_form` = 'https://www.qut.edu.au/courses/bachelor-of-biomedical-science-bachelor-of-mathematics', `course_description` = '<h4>Course Information</h4> <p>Combine your studies in biomedical science and mathematics to turn data analysis into real-world patient outcomes.Understanding data - how to analyse it, model it and make useful predictions from it - will continue to underpin new technologies, processes and discoveries in all areas of the economy.</p> <p>In the case of biomedicine, the increased capacity to generate large datasets from patients and or treatment regimens requires graduates with a capacity to understand both the biology and the mathematics.</p> <p>In the Bachelor of Biomedical Science you will study how the body works, investigate how disease or injury interferes with normal function, and treatment strategies that help restore function. You will also have a high degree of course flexibility with the option to select one major or two minor areas of study that align with your interests.</p> <p>In the Bachelor of Mathematics you will learn to be an agile problem solver, capable of tackling real-world problems in their full complexity, through the application of modern mathematical, statistical and computational approaches. Your specialist knowledge and skills in one of the contemporary specialisations of mathematical practice - applied and computational mathematics, statistics, and operations research - will be underpinned by a solid foundational base of mathematical training, and complemented by computational and programming skills.</p> <h5>Course Structure</h5> <p>Biomedical Science component consists of 96 credit points of core biomedical science studies and either one 72 credit point Biomedical Science Major and 24 credit points of elective units, or two Biomedical Science Minors (each worth 48 credit points).\n\nThe Mathematics component consists of 96 credit points of core units and 96 credit points of a selected major.</p>', `entry_requirements` = '<h4>English Language Requirements (International Students)</h4><ul><li><strong>IELTS Academic:</strong> IELTS Academic / One Skill Retake 6.5</li><li><strong>PTE Academic:</strong> PTE Academic 59</li></ul>', `english_requirements` = '<h4>English Language Requirements (International Students)</h4><ul><li><strong>IELTS Academic:</strong> IELTS Academic / One Skill Retake 6.5</li><li><strong>PTE Academic:</strong> PTE Academic 59</li></ul>', `total_course_duration` = '4 years full-time (208 weeks), 8 years part-time (416 weeks)', `assessment_style` = 'assignment', `intakes` = 'February', `updated_at` = '2026-11-02 16:20:46' WHERE `id` = 2617;
UPDATE `courses` SET `apply_form` = 'https://www.qut.edu.au/courses/graduate-certificate-in-business-analysis', `course_description` = '<h4>Course Information</h4> <p>If you want knowledge and skills in new technological trends, and are interested in developing the specialist knowledge and skills to succeed in senior IT-related positions, then this course is for you. The Graduate Certificate in Business Analysis focuses on the development of skills to allow you to critically analyse complex work environments, assess alternate information systems solutions, and evaluate outcomes.</p> <h5>Course Structure</h5> <p>48 credit points</p> <h5>Study & Career Pathways</h5> <p>The QUT Graduate Certificate in Business Analysis is located at Level 8 of the Australian Qualifications Framework (AQF). Graduates will be eligible for entry into IN20 Master of Information Technology with a reduced course duration.</p>', `entry_requirements` = '<h4>Academic Entry Requirements (International Students)</h4><ul><li>A recognised bachelor degree (or higher qualification) in information technology or related discipline; or a recognised bachelor degree (or higher qualification) in any discipline followed by at least three years full-time (or equivalent) professional experience in an information technology related field; or a recognised diploma (or higher qualification) in information technology or related discipline followed by at least two years full-time (or equivalent) professional work experience in an information technology related field; or at least five years full-time (or equivalent) professional work experience in an information technology field.</li></ul>', `total_course_duration` = '6 months full-time (26 weeks), 1 year part-time (52 weeks)', `assessment_style` = 'assignment', `intakes` = 'February; February, June, October; January; July; July, August, October; July, November; July. August. October. November; March, July, November; October; Start any time; Throughout the year', `updated_at` = '2026-11-02 16:20:46' WHERE `id` = 2618;
